  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Pennsylvania State University obligated $354M in FY2026 to date across 207 awards, with an average award size of $1.7M and year-over-year change up 2.6%. The Department of Defense obligated $351M for FY2026 to date, making defense-related work the dominant source of federal funds to Pennsylvania State University. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is the largest market, with $352M obligated in FY2026 to date. Obligations have increased across the tracked period, rising from $202M in FY21 to $354M in FY26. Other FY2026 buyers include the National Aeronautics and Space Administration with $2M and the Department of the Interior with $1.1M. Secondary NAICS markets in FY2026 to date include Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities at $469K and Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools at $70.8K. Some NAICS and agency lines show zero or small values in FY2026 to date, reflecting a concentration of obligations in a few buyers and markets.",
