      },
      {
        "heading": "What does Pennsylvania State University sell to the government?",
        "body": "Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences (except Nanotechnology and Biotechnology) is Pennsylvania State University’s largest market at $352M. Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $2M and Research and Development in the Social Sciences and Humanities accounted for $469K. Colleges, Universities, and Professional Schools accounted for $70.8K, with other NAICS categories at or near $0 in FY2026 to date."
